e>135</fpage><lpage>138</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10327187</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000435-McBride2"><label>52</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McBride</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Schulz-Schaeffer</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Donaldson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruce</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Diringer</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kretzschmar</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name><name><surname>Beekes</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Early spread of scrapie from the gastrointestinal tract to the central nervous system involves autonomic fibers of the splanchnic and vagus nerves.</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>75</volume><fpage>9320</fpage><lpage>9327</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11533195</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000435-Thomzig2"><label>53</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thomzig</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Schulz-Schaeffer</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Kratzel</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Mai</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Beekes</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Preclinical deposition of pathological prion protein PrPSc in muscles of hamsters orally exposed to scrapie.</article-title><source>J Clin Invest</source><volume>113</volume><fpage>1465</fpage><lpage>1472</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15146244</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000435-Foster1"><label>54</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Foster</surname><given-nam